WEBVTT

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.010
I fell asleep?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.870
Sh-Shinoaki?!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.210
Guess the sun's up.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.080
G'morning.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.700
Uh, good morning.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.660
<b>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPhotography
\h\h\h\h\h\hCollection
\h\h\h\hby
\h\hKuwa
 Mei</b>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.540
<b>Empty Space</b>

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.920
Oh, you came to check out reference material,
 and then fell asleep.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.300
Sorry for falling asleep like that.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.300
But I think I've got the right idea 
for what I wanna draw next!

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.220
That's good. I guess you'll 
be getting back to work...

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.140
Um...

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.110
<i>This... is confirmed now, right?</i>

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.310
Kyoya!

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.560
Breakfast is ready, so get your butt—

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.720
Wow. Pretty bold, aren't you?

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.320
Uh, it's not that, we were just—

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.750
Well, get a move on! Tsurayuki's waiting!

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.430
What do you reckon she's mad about?

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:13.110
Tsurayuki, the professor mentioned 
you'd been missing class lately.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.220
Yeah, I've been packing 
in the shifts at work lately.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.260
You sure you weren't just skipping class?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.970
What, like you? Stupid.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.180
It's rude to call people stupid, stupid!

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.740
Is that what it was? I was worried 
you weren't feeling too good.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.940
Nah, that's not it at all. 
I'm the picture of health.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.980
That's good.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.050
I'll be going to class more 
regularly starting next week.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.620
So tell the prof not to worry.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.860
Okay. Sure.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.680
<i>But in the following week, 
Tsurayuki didn't show up for class.</i>

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.100
I'm heading out!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.770
Let go of me already!

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.600
I sure as heck ain't!

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.010
What's going on, you two?

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.820
I said I was fine, but she 
won't shut up about getting rest!

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.480
How in tarnation are you fine?!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.190
You've been under th' weather
 all the time lately!

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.520
You <i>just</i> threw up in the bathroom!

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.940
I just ate too much yesterday!

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.400
Seriously, it's nothing, 
just stop worry...ing...

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:18.770
Tsurayuki!

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:19.860
Tsurayuki-kun!

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.800
Come on! Hang in there, Tsurayuki!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.810
See? I told you, it was nothing.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.050
How exactly is sleep deprivation 
and burnout from work nothing?

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.720
The doctor said you needed 
to get plenty of bed rest!

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.890
And to not do any work that involves 
physical activity for the foreseeable future.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.930
Sorry for dragging you out here.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.730
You don't need to worry any more, though.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.140
Tsurayuki, what are you so on edge about?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.480
It's weird. You're working 
yourself to death.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.410
It's none of your business.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.520
Why not? Tell me the reason.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.660
I might be able to help!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.630
How the hell are you gonna do that?!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.640
Sorry for yelling, man.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.320
Look... I'm fighting with my parents.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.840
I've been paying my tuition myself.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.100
I come from a long line of doctors, 
so they want me to be one, too.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.850
I ran out because I didn't want to do that.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.960
And with that kind of background, 
I couldn't get a scholarship.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.300
So I took on as much work as I could.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.480
But I guess if I have to ditch class for work, 
I'm putting the cart in front of the horse.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.650
I managed to rebel against my 
parents for this long, but...

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:48.410
I think my little struggle for independence 
has gone as far as it can.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:53.000
If I can't pay my tuition, and can't work,
 then I can't do anything.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.600
I've got nothing left.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.840
There's just no way.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.550
<i>There's no way?</i>

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.510
<i>There </i>has<i> to be!</i>

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:12.030
<i>I know there has to be something! Think!</i>

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.560
There is something.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.150
A way for you to make money on your own.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.280
You are seriously something, man!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.210
Whenever we think something 
is a lost cause, you flip it around...

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.910
And somehow manage to pull it off.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.100
But I'm telling you...

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.610
That this is no joke, all right?

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:42.550
You're dealing with something I don't want 
other people messing with right now!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.510
When you say this is possible, 
do you realize that?!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.550
I do.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.930
It doesn't look like it!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.740
I'm not just tossing out a theory here.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.560
I have a plan.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.240
You actually have an idea?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.350
Yeah.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.410
I do.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:16.210
We'll figure it out. 
We really will, damn it!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.260
We're all...

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.300
...going to make...

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.410
...a game?

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.450
That's right.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:58.330
Like, the kind you play on a console?

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.520
What we're going to make is a doujin game, 
and they're usually played on PCs.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.360
Doujin game?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.270
Right.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.750
It's not like games made by businesses 
and distributed to retailers.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:11.530
Individuals work together to make them... 
And then sell them at direct market events.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.660
Oh, I get it, like indie music.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.620
And we're going to be making a novel game,

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.240
which uses text and images 
for a sort of picture show.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.350
That way, we won't need a lot 
of technical expertise, plus...

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.830
I get you!

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.620
And I'm going to write the script?

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.340
Exactly!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.750
Shinoaki can do the illustrations.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.280
And Nanako will handle the background music.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.390
Sure thing! Sounds like fun!

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.770
But I've hardly composed anything before.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.830
I'll teach you how, along with how 
to use the equipment involved.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:49.450
I'm going to be the director, 
so I'll be there to back you all up.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:54.100
Having you manage everything 
is a big relief, Kyoya-kun!

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.780
Well, if Kyoya-kun's in charge, 
that's reassuring.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:01.210
I'm sorry to drag you all into my business!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.920
You don't need to worry none.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.900
Man, I've never seen 
Tsurayuki grateful before!

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:08.880
I'm deducting my gratitude toward you.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.970
Why?! You should give me extra, in fact!

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.390
Whatcha need?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.600
You decided to finally help our circle out?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.850
I'm sorry. Not exactly...

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.350
I wanted to ask you about something important.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.450
Damn, you seem pretty serious.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.200
You get into some kinda trouble, kid?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.650
Or didja mess around with the wrong gal?

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.110
I need to earn some money!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.280
Gimme the details.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.250
I get ya...

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.840
That does seem like you'd 
needta put a rush on it.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:53.220
Right. Tuition is due by May, 
so before then...

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:58.110
Making money offa doujin 
games ain't easy, though.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.910
You kids might be talented, 
but the trick to selling this kinda stuff

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:04.230
is having a big name attached.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.820
I know. That's what I'm asking 
to borrow from you.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.510
I getcha.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:14.560
You wanna put your game out 
as a new release from Hallucigenia Soft?

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.130
I realize how presumptuous this is.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.240
But... it's the only solution I can think of.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:25.730
All right. You can use our name.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.820
Really?! Thank you so much!

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.120
But in exchange...

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.770
I've got some stipulations.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:33.940
You do?

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.470
<i>It has to be something 
that will sell well, huh?</i>

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.470
<i>That's a simple request, but a tough one.</i>

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:46.760
<i>It's ten years in the past, so the urban 
fantasy trend has just about run its course.</i>

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.620
<i>What came after that?</i>

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.940
<i>It has to be easy to understand, simple to 
conceive of, but steadfastly popular.</i>

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.190
Okay!

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.030
A school story?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.270
And that is...

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:02.320
<i>Right! I need to explain that part, too.</i>

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.270
Well, school stories are...

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:08.580
Stories that take place 
in and surrounding a school.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:12.330
So it's super literal? 
Still not sure I get it.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:15.690
Shouldn't there be like, 
monsters and stuff, too?

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:18.290
I don't think that would be 
a good idea at this stage.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:23.210
I can't be certain, but there's 
a good chance it wouldn't sell.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.580
So it's a question of popularity.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.710
In that case, I guess I get it.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.900
Now, most games with school stories 
tend to focus on romance.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.570
R-Romance?!

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.900
Are you okay?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.150
T-Totally fine!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.610
Continue, by all means.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.210
There are also sexy scenes where—

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.410
Sex?!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.410
I-Is there a problem?

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:54.990
Kyoya!

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:58.310
You're talking about like... 
actual scenes where people do it, right?

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.300
I am. That's a part of it.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:09.030
To be honest with you, I don't have 
any of that kind of experience.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.680
That kind as in...

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.080
Oh! I-It's fine!

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:18.010
There are professional writers who deal 
with that kind of material without any experience.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.090
You mean it?!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:22.150
Yeah! So, don't worry.

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:23.420
I see...

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.280
Man, what am I gonna do?

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:30.780
So I think we should make a school story.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.100
Teacher, question!

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:32.710
What is it?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.750
I've never played games like that before.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.590
So I'm not really sure what one's like.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.340
Oh, me neither.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.090
You want to try one?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.390
I have some installed on this laptop.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.800
O-Okay, we'll go check it out.

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:49.980
Come on!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:50.770
Okay!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.890
Wh-What is that?!

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:00.590
What's wrong?

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.830
That cute girl showed up...

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.350
But then there was all that stuff, 
and they did something crazy!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.740
I was so shocked and embarrassed!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:09.080
Nanako, that hurts!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.410
What the heck was that?! Seriously!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:13.000
I don't really get what was going on, 
but the game seems fun.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:13.820
Ow!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.540
It was way more extreme than "fun"!

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.560
Kyoya, you stupid pervert! 
I have no idea what's wrong with you!

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.300
<i>This isn't going to be easy...</i>

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:31.020
<i>But I can't give up.</i>

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.060
<i>I'm the only one who can help Tsurayuki.</i>

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:39.660
Hashiba!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.400
Care to join me for lunch?

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.710
Sorry, I've got to meet somebody!

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.290
How do you know 
about this guy anyway, Hashy?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.460
I happened to see his work
 at the school festival.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.360
And I thought he'd be perfect...

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.960
I'm amazed you remember
 something like that.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:03.470
<i>Well, what I really remember is his name 
from ten years in the future.</i>

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.890
I'm the club president, 
Yamashina. Nice to meet you.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.540
I'm Hashiba.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.260
I'll get right to the point.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:14.280
I'd like you to handle the backgrounds 
for our doujin game.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:15.910
That sounds great.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:20.540
I can't do character art, so my work 
doesn't get a lot of attention.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.610
<i>That settles that! Next is equipment!</i>

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.860
Thank you very much!

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.640
I heard they opened 
a big Yodobushi in Umeda,

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.700
but if you want actual parts, 
nothing beats Ponbashi.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.580
I'm amazed at how much we bought.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.100
Well, when you're making a game,

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.510
it pays to make sure you've got beefy hardware.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.150
Otherwise...

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.990
Is something wrong?

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:46.700
Get a load of that.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.180
She definitely stands out, doesn't she?

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:54.090
You figure some li'l princess is out 
buying doujinshi in secret?

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:57.040
I doubt it. Anyway, Keiko-san, 
didn't you have more shopping?

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.080
Oh, good point! Let's get a move on.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.740
I see...

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.610
I didn't realize that Rokuonji 
was in that kind of situation.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:13.490
Right, which is why we're all 
working together to support him.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.910
You are? This isn't any kind 
of shady work, is it?

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.100
N-No, don't worry!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:23.750
<i>I'm not sure what she'd say if I told her 
we're working on a doujin game.</i>

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:27.050
I thought you might do something like 
borrow the name of a famous circle

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.050
to try and sell a doujin game 
that you're making.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.350
What's wrong?

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:35.880
Uh, Sensei, where did you hear about that?

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.640
Doncha know that honesty's the best policy?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.590
K-Keiko-san?!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:49.400
So the two of you have worked 
on games together before?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.940
Right. I'm retired, though.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.940
Kanou-chan was a big help back in the day!

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:59.800
And if her student's in trouble, 
I figure it's the least I could do to help!

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:03.520
Is that it? Because I thought you were 
interested in turning a profit.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.460
I mean, the cash 
is a separate issue altogether!

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.880
I think I'll choose to believe in
the more admirable motivation.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:13.930
Well, Keiko's explained what's 
going on with your game dev,

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.720
but don't let it interfere 
too much with your studies.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.400
It's okay, then?

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.810
Every aspect of production 
is going to aid in your education.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.120
I think it'll be a good experience.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.950
How's it coming along, anyway?

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:29.530
Smooth sailing so far?

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.560
W-Well... sure.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.520
I don't get it!

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.070
What's wrong?

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:46.970
I've been playing that game 
you lent me as a sample.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.730
All of those girls, for no reason 
and with no impetus,

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:53.640
are in love with me 
as soon as the game begins!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.180
What's up with that?!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.760
That's just how it goes. 
Try to understand.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.280
Okay, but even if I'm willing to accept that,

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.220
what's with their speech?!

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:04.640
"Takumi-kun, I hope you had 
a meowy good day at work!"

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.400
Who talks like that?!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.690
It's just how these things go...

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:11.190
Kyoya...

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.820
N-Nanako?!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.460
I don't get it.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:20.000
I have no idea how composing 
on a computer works.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.070
What's going on there?

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:24.120
Instead of a musical score, 
there are these weird bars.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.670
I know it might be confusing at first,

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.040
but once you get used to it, 
it's easier! Okay?

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:31.540
You sure?

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:34.510
Kyoya-kun!

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:38.280
Art for games is tough, huh?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.220
Shinoaki!

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.940
Please... Please, refer to the 
sample art I gave you! Okay?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.940
<i>This is about the furthest possible 
thing from smooth sailing.</i>

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:59.200
Control the centrifugal force 
by keeping your left wrist steady.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:03.850
<i>I got hardly any sleep last night.</i>

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:05.570
Shinoaki?

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.030
Shinoaki!

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:12.870
I'm a little sleepy...

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.470
More than a little! Be careful—

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.970
Nanako?!

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.920
I dozed off...

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.310
Here, let me wipe that off!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:31.110
What's up, Kyoya? Everything going okay?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:34.700
You're the one not doing okay! 
What are you even making?!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.620
Hey, you're right. My bad.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:41.830
That group over there! 
What are you all doing?!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.870
Sorry!

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:46.120
What is going on?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:50.890
You've all been half-asleep through 
both your general education and arts classes.

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:53.800
Sorry... there's a good reason.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.760
I bet there is. I'd really 
let you have it, otherwise.

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.380
So?

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:00.940
Well...

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.920
I see. That is rough.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.080
Could you keep it quiet, though?

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.800
It's not the kind of thing you 
want to spread around.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.160
Of course.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:16.320
So? What can I do to help?

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.290
That's what you need, right?

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:21.530
If there's anything I can contribute,
 just let me know.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.550
Thanks! I really appreciate it!

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.810
The first thing that comes to mind...

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.660
There are issues with the 
script and art direction...

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.540
There's also the progress on the opening...

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.150
Okay, I'm catching a bus.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:36.150
Yeah. Thanks for offering your advice.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.000
See you around.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:42.220
Hashiba...

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:47.190
You're a competent worker, 
and you're smart enough,

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.180
but it seems to me like 
you might be overdoing it.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.060
Are you... really okay?

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:56.970
Yeah. It's not a problem.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:59.790
Okay... if you say so.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.230
All right...

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:17.820
Kyoya, check this section for me.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:18.800
Okay.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.630
I think the writing might 
be a little stiff, still.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:28.310
Still? I thought I had fixed that,
 for the most part.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.590
Considering the genre, 
it needs to be a bit more loose.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.790
I also think there might be too 
much narration, relatively speaking.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.420
I'd like you to increase 
the amount of dialogue.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:37.640
Seriously?!

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:41.510
But... if you say so. I'll get on that, then.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.530
Sorry. I appreciate it.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.640
Dinner's ready!

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:47.070
Coming!

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.430
Tsurayuki?

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.290
Sorry. I'll be along in a sec.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.800
<b>Are you sure you want to delete?</b>

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.800
<b>Delete</b>

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.800
<b>Cancel</b>

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.310
<b>Are you sure you want to delete?</b>

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.310
<b>Delete</b>

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.310
<b>Cancel</b>

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:20.110
Y'know, the other day, 
I saw the strangest-looking folks.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:21.490
You did?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.560
It was over in the school parking lot.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:29.440
This big old black car pulls up, 
and out comes a big fella in a black suit,

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:33.350
and this cute gal in a fur coat!

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:36.280
I wonder if they're students.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:39.920
What the heck? Sounds like a yakuza princess.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:45.100
Now that you mention it, I think 
I might've seen the same people.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:49.680
Shinoaki... was this girl 
wearing a white beret?

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:51.720
Yeah, she was.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.160
W-With short hair?

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.900
And a sorta, general vibe 
of being a rich girl?

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.150
Did you notice that?!

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.440
H-Hey, Tsurayuki, what's gotten into...

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:12.850
Guys, sorry, but I need 
to make myself scarce for today!

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:14.510
Wait, why?!

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:16.120
I'll explain when I get back!

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.630
I knew this was the place!

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:25.520
It's her!

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.060
S-Sayuri-nee...

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.140
Tsu-kun! It's been ages!

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.430
I missed you so much!

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.930
G-Get off! Seriously, Sayuri-nee, let me go!

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:36.700
Why, though?

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:39.910
Shouldn't we smooch now, 
to celebrate our reunion?

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.130
Come on, Tsu-kun!

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.130
Hang on a...

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:52.790
It's a pleasure to meet you all. 
My name is Jisshoji Sayuri.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:56.410
I am Rokuonji Tsurayuki-san's...

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.040
Fiancée!

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.540
F... F... F...

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:03.170
Fiancée?!
